1. For the negative test case, why are floor() and trunc() different?
Floor() will always round down to negative infinity, while trunc() simply removes the decimal. 
2. Which function is best when you need the nearest integer rather than always moving up, down, or toward zero?
Round() is best because it will always round towards 0.
3. Why is fabs() more suitable than simply removing the minus sign manually?
Because it will just et the negative sign when the integer is <0.
